 Signature |language=en-US}}</ref> It is prepared without cooking, hence the name 'coldmeal'.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*[[Cookbook:Dryfish|Nigerian smoked dried fish]]\n*[[Cookbook:Onion|Onions]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] and rinsed\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] garri ([[Cookbook:Cassava Flour|cassava flour]])\n*1 [[Cookbook:Kuli Kuli|kuli kuli]], ground\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n*Dry pepper to taste\n==Procedure==\n#Mash the smoked fish in a bowl.\n#Add the garri, ground kuli kuli, sliced onions, salt, and dry pepper.\n#Stir the ingredients together and serve.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* You can add some water to moisten the garri if desired.\n\n== References ==\n[[Category:Nigerian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cassava flour]]\n<references />\n[[Category:Recipes using dryfish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Kwado (Nigerian Cassava Flour Salad)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Nigerian smoked dried fish","sourceText":"Nigerian smoked dried fish","amountText":"Nigerian smoked dried fish","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Onions, sliced and rinsed","sourceText":"Onions, sliced and rinsed","amountText":"Onions, sliced and rinsed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 cups garri (cassava flour)","sourceText":"2 cups garri (cassava flour)","amountText":"2 cups garri (cassava flour)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 kuli kuli, ground","sourceText":"1 kuli kuli, ground","amountText":"1 kuli kuli, ground","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Salt to taste","sourceText":"Salt to taste","amountText":"Salt to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Dry pepper to taste","sourceText":"Dry pepper to taste","amo